{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed sub-division would result in the loss of 3 family-sized dwellings&nbsp;which is a priority house type within the Borough.&nbsp;As such, the proposal is considered unacceptable and contrary to the following:Policy BC4 of the Borough Wide DPD (March 2011)Policies SP 3 and DMH 5 of the&nbsp;Draft Local Plan Regulation 19 Main Modifications Version (February 2024).",
    "The development constitutes phased development. Without the submission of sufficient evidence the lack of affordable housing provision on site has not been justified. Noting the lack of affordable housing provision the proposed development is therefore considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:Chapter 5 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2023)Policies H4, H5 and H6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy CC1 of the Core Strategy DPD (July 2010)Policy BC1 of the Borough Wide DPD (March 2011)Policy DHM1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Main Modifications Version, February 2024)",
    "the proposed development would present a sub-standard quality of accommodation especially for three of the flats as they would fail to meet the NDSS thus downgrading the quality of&nbsp;the existing&nbsp;flats. As such, the proposal is considered unacceptable and contrary to the following:Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy BP6 of the Borough Wide DPD (March 2011)DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)Housing Design Standards London Planning Guidance (June 2023)",
    "The proposed development has the potential to increase activity level and coming and goings to and from the site leading to additional levels of noise and disturbance at the property. This is considered to have a negative impact on amenity of neighbouring properties and in turn the health and wellbeing of neighbouring residents. As such the proposal is contrary to the following:Policies BP8 and BP11 of the Borough Wide DPD (March 2011).Policies DMD 1, SP 7 and DMSI 3 of the Draft Local Plan Regulation 19 Main Modifications Version (February 2024).",
    "In the absence of a parking stress survey insufficient evidence has been submitted to confirm the proposed car parking arrangement&nbsp;would be sufficient to support the needs of the development and have an acceptable impact on the highway and on-street parking amenity.&nbsp;The proposed development is therefore considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:Chapter 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2023)Policy T6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy&nbsp;BR11&nbsp;the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policy DMT 2 the&nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Main Modifications Version, February 2024)"
  ],
